---
// Benchmark results, shown on the homepage and on What's new in 2.x.
// Bars: best pass, worst pass (as a share of the slowest pass for that metric), label.
const metrics = [
	{ label: 'Startup', v1: ['100%', '100%', '6.2 s'], v2: ['6.5%', '8.1%', '0.4–0.5 s'] },
	{ label: 'CPU time per GB streamed', v1: ['99.2%', '100%', '13.2–13.3 s'], v2: ['27.8%', '30.8%', '3.7–4.1 s'] },
	{ label: 'Memory at idle', v1: ['54.6%', '100%', '165–302 MB'], v2: ['22.5%', '23.2%', '68–70 MB'] },
	{ label: 'Memory per stream', v1: ['83.7%', '100%', '1.28–1.53 GB'], v2: ['74.5%', '82.4%', '1.14–1.26 GB'] },
];
---

<p>Lower is better. Bars show the range across three passes.</p>

<div class="not-content perf">
	{
		metrics.map(({ label, v1, v2 }) => (
			<div class="perf-metric">
				<p class="perf-label">{label}</p>
				{[['1.x', v1], ['2.x', v2]].map(([version, [min, max, value]]) => (
					<div class:list={['perf-row', { 'is-next': version === '2.x' }]}>
						<span class="perf-version">{version}</span>
						<span class="perf-track" aria-hidden="true">
							<span class="perf-bar" style={{ '--min': min, '--max': max }} />
						</span>
						<span class="perf-value">{value}</span>
					</div>
				))}
			</div>
		))
	}
</div>

<p>
	Sequential throughput is on par within run-to-run variance: 103–111 MB/s on 1.x, 92–103 MB/s on 2.x. Neither version
	rebuffered in five plays at a 3.1 MB/s playback rate.
</p>

<p class="perf-method">
	Measured on 27 October 2026 with 1.6.3 and 2.0.0-alpha.8 in Docker on one Apple M4 Pro host, one commercial provider
	with 20 connections, five posts with a median size of 10.7 GB, three passes.
</p>
